  "result": "I implemented the constructor and `resolvedOptions` for `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, but not formatting. `intl402/DateTimeFormat/` is at 184 of 342 runs passing; clippy is clean. The remaining 158 failures are all from the unimplemented methods, and none are crashes or wrong results.\n\n- **Done:** `CreateDateTimeFormat`, `ChainDateTimeFormat`, `UnwrapDateTimeFormat` and the internal slots (in `support/intl_date_time_format.rs`). Time zone lookup and hour-cycle defaults come from ICU4X.\n- **Still `not_implemented`:** `get format`, `formatToParts`, `formatRange` and `formatRangeToParts`. Formatting needs the mapping from the component options to an ICU4X field set, which I didn't get to. The `format` getter alone accounts for 52 of the failing runs.\n- **Stand-ins:** `BasicFormatMatcher`, `BestFitFormatMatcher` and `DateTimeStyleFormat` are not implemented. The requested components are used as the format, so `resolvedOptions` reports what was asked for rather than the pattern ICU4X would pick. For `dateStyle`/`timeStyle`, `resolvedOptions` reports no components.\n- **Simplified locale data:** the calendar list is a hardcoded list of ICU4X calendars with `gregory` first. `numberingSystem` is `latn` only. The default hour cycle is probed by formatting a time with ICU4X.\n\nBLOCKED: formatting (`format`, `formatToParts`, `formatRange`, `formatRangeToParts`) needs the component-options \u2192 ICU4X field-set and time zone mapping, which I did not implement.",
